# This file is a placeholder. The private key has been removed from version control
# because committing private keys is a security risk (CWE-798).
#
# To provide a TLS private key at runtime:
#   1. Set TLS key-related environment variables (TLS_KEYSTORE, TLS_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD), or
#   2. Mount a volume containing the key file at this path, or
#   3. Use keystore.sh to regenerate the keystore from a locally generated key (do not commit).
#
# IMPORTANT: The previously committed private key must be rotated (revoked and
# reissued) because it remains in the git history.
